If $\|Tx\|\ge\delta\|x\|$ and $Tx_n\to y$, then $x_n$ is Cauchy, so $x_n\to x$ and $y=Tx$; the range is closed. Conversely a closed range is Banach, and $T:X\to T(X)$ has bounded inverse by the <Open mapping theorem>, giving the lower bound. This is the <Closed-range criterion for an injection>.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

