$$
But $\mathbb P(X_n/n>1)=\mathbb P(X_1>n)\sim1/(\pi n)$. These independent-event probabilities have divergent sum, so the second <Borel-Cantelli lemmas> says $X_n/n>1$ infinitely often almost surely, a contradiction.

