{parent=ii}

See <Analysis>.

For $\deg p\le2n-1$, divide $p=q p_n+r$ with $\deg q\le n-1$, $\deg r\le n-1$. Orthogonality makes $\int qp_n=0$, and $p(t_j)=r(t_j)$. Apply part (i) to $r$. This is <Gaussian quadrature>.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= iii
{parent=2i}
